---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
  business,
  marketingAvailability,
  marketingPrograms,
  noticeVersions,
  providers,
  retentionPolicy,
} from '../data/business';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="SMS Terms"
  description="The intended terms for Sapphire Blue automated marketing texts. The SMS program is not active and is not accepting subscriptions."
  version={noticeVersions.sms}
>
  <div class="notice">
    <p><strong>SMS status: {marketingAvailability.sms ? 'enabled' : 'disabled — not accepting subscriptions'}.</strong></p>
    <p>This page describes a planned program, not an active sign-up offer. A verifiable permission register and operational SMS setup have not been implemented. Providing a phone number in a business inquiry does not subscribe you.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Operator and intended sender</h2>
  <p>
    {business.brand} is operated by {business.operator}, {business.operatorDescription}.
    The intended brand and sender identity for this program is {business.brand}, using {providers.marketing.name} as the proposed delivery provider.
    No operational SMS program number or sender has been established for this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    For questions, contact Asor at <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>.
    The site is intended for {business.initialAudience}.
  </p>

  <h2>What the planned messages would cover</h2>
  <p>{marketingPrograms.sms.purpose} {marketingPrograms.sms.frequency} {marketingPrograms.sms.charges}</p>
  <p>
    These would be commercial messages from {business.brand}, not a requirement for ordinary business correspondence.
    There is no currently operating automated SMS service or delivery commitment under these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>A separate, optional choice</h2>
  <p>
    If launched, automated marketing texts would require a separate, optional SMS opt-in supported by a verifiable permission record.
    Choosing email marketing would not also choose SMS, and choosing SMS would not also choose email.
    Permission would not be a condition of purchasing services, receiving a quote or sending an inquiry.
  </p>
  <p>
    The phone field in the current inquiry form is for contact about the request, not an SMS marketing enrollment mechanism.
    Neither the existence of this page nor submitting that form activates a subscription.
  </p>

  <h2>Intended opt-out and help — not operational</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>STOP</strong> is the intended SMS opt-out command for a future launch.
    There is currently no configured program number, operational STOP handler or operational HELP workflow for this site.
    Do not rely on texting STOP or HELP now, or send them to an unverified number expecting an automated response.
  </p>
  <p>
    Until the program is configured, email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> for questions or a manual request about information you have already shared.
    {business.operator} handles these requests manually. No automated SMS support or response-time guarantee is offered.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before any launch, the sender identity, opt-out and help instructions, permission records and handling of withdrawals must be configured and verified,
    and these terms must be reviewed to reflect the actual program.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and records</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="/privacy">Privacy &amp; Cookies</a> for the operator, current providers, access from the Dominican Republic and United States,
    optional website measurement, intended retention and manual privacy requests.
    {providers.marketing.name} is planned only and is not part of the current contact-processing integration.
  </p>
  <p>
    For a future program, only the relevant phone number, subscription choices and evidence needed to manage permission and opt-outs should be used for enrollment.
    The intended retention for {retentionPolicy.permissions.record.toLowerCase()} is: {retentionPolicy.permissions.period.toLowerCase()}
    That is a retention target, not an implemented permission register or automatic deletion system.
  </p>
  <p>
    The version label on this page identifies its wording only. It does not demonstrate that an opt-in was collected or verified.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
